 "buyers_guide": [
  {
   "q": "Presence sensor or motion sensor?",
   "a": "A motion sensor (PIR) sees movement, so lights turn off if you sit still. An mmWave presence sensor detects breathing-level motion, so it knows you're still in the room while you read or work."
  },
  {
   "q": "Do presence sensors need power?",
   "a": "Most mmWave sensors need USB or wall power because the radar runs constantly. A few newer battery models combine PIR and mmWave to save power."
  },
  {
   "q": "Can it tell where I am in the room?",
   "a": "Some models, like the Aqara FP2, support zones, so a desk, couch, and bed can trigger different automations."
  }
 ],
